    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — 8 PASS, 11 FAIL.\n\n**Summary of findings:**\n\nThe app's search, model browsing, metrics computation, and gap alerting work well. The core defect cluster is in the graph editor: `CompetencyGraph` initializes React Flow with `useNodesState(initialNodes)` and never re-syncs, so node cards, disabled states, critical-path highlighting, and the graph itself never reflect model changes — and stale callbacks make each edit overwrite prior edits (e.g. a level change silently re-enabled a disabled competency).\n\nKey failures:\n- **FT-4** – relationship weights are displayed but have no editing affordance at all.\n- **FT-5 / IX-20 / CT-16 / FT-7** – graph never updates: no disabled styling, competencies can't be re-enabled, node values stay stale, critical-path highlighting contradicts the summary, and applying a template leaves the old graph in place.\n- **FT-8 / FT-11** – \"Save Current\" and \"Save\" only fire toasts; no name/description form, no My Templates, no persistence.\n- **IX-19** – the pre-selected Recruitment scenario starts with empty adjustments, so running it does nothing until you switch tabs.\n- **FT-10 / CS-12** – picking a custom category adjustment leaves the paired delta undefined, yielding \"NaN%\" weight change and a corrupted **Coverage NaN%**."
  }
}
